      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I am not really sure but I assume it's related to memory leaks that I have been experiencing since the update.\nI have been staying online overnight in over a year and after the latest patch I started notice that either my RAM or VRAM gets capped to the max.\nso far 1 time it happened with RAM\nand 2 times with capped VRAM\nsystem is CPU - i7 8086k , GPU- 1080ti 11G, RAM 32G, VR is Oculus CV1\nlatest drivers on all components\nBefore I leave the system I play vrc like normal, then I just leave the headset like I have always been until now overnight.\nNext day I go back in vr, VRAM is maxed out, when turn on mirror it's black and when I switch avatar it does not render at all and the PC just feels laggy as a whole.\nworld I AFK in is Alekso's Hangout map: wrld_edf6fa08-d7ac-49a3-9c3e-986b34d0721d\nSame routine as always before I go afk - I turn off everything from the side pannel and I go to the culled area behind the mirror and leave my vr 8 to 12h.\nI hope that's related to the case and gives off any hints. \nGood luck fixing it o/",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
